        "original_id": "7b592dc0-088f-5e29-85de-ee48fbf0f144",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: NGC 166, PGC 2143\n- People: Francis Preserved Leavenworth, Frank Muller, Ormond Stone\n- Places: Cetus\n- Topics: spiral galaxies, New General Catalogue objects\n\nFacts:\n- In 1886, Francis Preserved Leavenworth discovered NGC 166.\n- Francis Preserved Leavenworth discovered many New General Catalogue objects together with Frank Muller and Ormond Stone.\n- NGC 166 is also known as PGC 2143.\n- NGC 166 is a spiral galaxy in the constellation Cetus.\n- NGC 166 is located around 2.6 million light-years away.\n- NGC 166 has an apparent magnitude of 15.18.",
